Qt / PySide6 (LGPL-3.0)
-----------------------
The bundled GUI toolkit (Qt, via PySide6) is used under the terms of the
GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3 (LGPL-3.0); the license texts are in
the "Third-Party Licenses" tab of Help > Licenses and in third_party_license.txt. The Qt libraries
are separate files in the application folder (the PySide6 folder inside _internal,
or inside the macOS app bundle), not compiled into the program, and the
application loads them at runtime, so they can be replaced with a compatible build
of the same Qt version. Nothing in the license of Teacher's Teammate restricts
changing the application for your own use or reverse engineering it to debug such
changes. The complete source code of Teacher's Teammate is publicly available at
https://github.com/JoHoenk/teachers-teammate.

The build carries only the Qt modules the app uses. Qt Charts and the other modules that Qt offers
only under the GPL-3.0 or a commercial license stay out because nothing uses them, and the smoke
test fails if one is still in the finished bundle.

FFmpeg inside OpenCV (LGPL-2.1)
-------------------------------
The OpenCV package (opencv-python-headless) carries FFmpeg. It is used under the GNU Lesser
General Public License, version 2.1, whose text is in the OpenCV entry of the third-party
license list. The application never reads video. FFmpeg ships in the Linux and macOS bundles
only: the Windows bundle leaves out the separate DLL that OpenCV's Windows build carries.

Source code
-----------
The source of Teacher's Teammate itself is the "Source code" archive on the page of each release
(https://github.com/JoHoenk/teachers-teammate/releases).

The LGPL and MPL components above are open source, and this section says where their source
is. The Qt, PySide6, FFmpeg and OpenCV entries name the version they were written for; a bump
turns the license test red until the entry and the sources release below name the new one.
certifi needs none: MPL-2.0 asks that its source be named, and every certifi release on PyPI
carries it.

Qt 6.12.0 and PySide6 6.12.0, the versions the bundle carries:
  https://download.qt.io/archive/qt/6.12/6.12.0/submodules/
      (qtbase, qtsvg, qtimageformats, qtwayland)
  https://download.qt.io/official_releases/QtForPython/pyside6/PySide6-6.12.0-src/

FFmpeg 9.0.2, inside opencv-python-headless 5.1.0.95 (Linux and macOS):
  https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-9.0.2.tar.gz
  The wheel's build recipe: https://github.com/opencv/opencv-python (tag 95)

certifi (MPL-2.0), the version Help > Licenses lists:
  https://pypi.org/project/certifi/

The same sources, as one download, are published with this release:
  https://github.com/JoHoenk/teachers-teammate/releases/tag/third-party-sources-qt6.12.0
It holds the four Qt modules above, pyside-setup at the matching tag, the FFmpeg tarball with its
signature and the opencv-python-headless source. It is never the "latest" release, so the app's
update check does not see it.

